The [old incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says “One issue, one fix queued.”
The rendered cause table contradicts that claim. Reports merged into #4471 cover two independent failures.
A parser fix alone does not correct the booking-form hint failure.
Counts below use the 4 October export. The later course engineering update reports #4471 closed on 5 October:
the parser was fixed, while the hint was closed as **won’t fix** because **booking-v3 was retired**.
Both outcomes appear in the computed disposition table; no production deployment was tested by this review.

## Tickets and counts

<SplitFindings />

### Parser: month-first interpretation of day-first tenant dates

The shared parser treats dates as month/day even when the tenant writes day/month.
This affects app and email intake, plus booking-v2 form reports, across the tenant directory.
For example, R-41200 from harbour.dental reports 7 April turning into 4 July.
Preserve the tenant's date order when parsing and test ambiguous dates in both directions.
The five one-day descriptions remain footnoted in this group rather than becoming a third ticket on symptoms alone.

### Hint: booking-v3 prints the wrong input order

For day-first tenants, booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while its form reads the tenant's day-first order.
A person following that hint supplies a month-first date which is interpreted the other way around.
Affected form reports belong to alder.physio (`de-DE`), copper.studio (`es-ES`), and pale.harbour (`pt-PT`).
For example, R-41230 is copper.studio/form: its browser locale and intake parser tag do not identify its cause.
A hint correction would need to agree with the actual parser and tenant locale. Engineering instead retired booking-v3,
so the hint ticket is closed as **not planned**, not as a shipped fix.

## Count causes, not intake guesses

Use `uniqueById`, then filter `mergedInto === 4471`, resolve each tenant from the directory, and run `causeOf`.
That function asks the platform for the tenant's date order; do not substitute a hand-maintained country list.
Neither a matching subject nor a browser locale proves two reports share a cause.
The CSV in `evidence/report-classification.csv` records every unique ID and its assigned cause.
The issue drafts contain each group's complete ID list, counts, examples, and acceptance checks.

## The desk's timeline

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports arrived before the desk's bulk merge and continued afterward. The desk's July merge activity is not an onset date.
Keep received and merged timestamps separate when judging trends, and do not interpret “known” as “fixed”.

## Replace the old dedupe policy

The [accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is historical and remains unedited.
Its subject-only rule can merge different causes and separate reports of the same cause.
The [replacement proposal 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) groups by verified failure path instead.
The old triage page was reviewed in 2024; its prose is stale even though its live component already compares causes.
The explorer below demonstrates both directions of the mismatch. Missing tenant information must stay unplaced until investigated.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Desk actions

Keep one engineering ticket for each cause, with a report count and evidence.
Route future reports using tenant locale, form version, and channel; read the body to confirm the failure path.
Keep unknown cases separate, record the uncertainty, and ask for the missing tenant or reproduction detail.
Recompute the groups when a new export arrives. Keep the two closure reasons distinct: the parser fix is completed;
the retired form’s hint is not planned. Do not claim that both bugs were fixed because the parent ticket is closed.
The new decision is a proposal for desk approval, not a claim that the desk has adopted it.

